Not necessarily.  The BC-p607P-BC tags were how the Software
Distribution Center named parts.  If I were submitting a 
set of tapes to the SDC for distribution, one part naming 
convention would be to bump up each tape part number _even
though the contents of the tapes hadn't changed from the
previous submission_.  The only way that a part number didn't
get bumped up with a submission is if, and only if, that tape
belonged to another product.  SDC part numbering and SPDs
(Software Product Description) were cross referenced in the 
bowels of the paper trails.  It isn't easy to describe in
ASCII English; AFAICT, there were only two, maybe three,
people who knew how to think in SDC-style when creating the
BOMs (bill of materials) for a submission.  
