>point as off-topic as the number of tape marks between files.

NO.  The tape marks have to do with how the tape was saved and
how the installation procedures expect to read the tape.  On
TOPS-10, we shipped things in a save set.  Each save set was
ended by a double soft tape mark.  (There are hard tape marks.)
To PIP a file off tape, you need a double soft tape mark.  That
denotes a logical tape file.  The contents of that logical file
may consist of more than one real file.
<snip>

I did not do RT-11 packaging and they may have changed their
rules, as we (TOPS-10) had changed ours over the years.  I'll
guarantee you that, by V5.01, there was a reason for everything.
Some of those reasons may have disappeared, but traditions 
always last longer.  

/BAH

