> This are the boards that seem to have something to do with graphics:
> M7169 - QDSS base board
> M7168 - QDSS 4 plane graphics board
> 
> What does "4 plane" mean?
> 
> Thanks in advance,
>    Sebastian


4 plane means that each pixel in the display is backed by four bits,
allowing 16 concurrent colors on the display.

This can either be set up as a color display or as a grey scale display.

The internal cable that goes from the card to the bulkhead is the key. 
It can be wired for either color or monochrome.  If your external cable
does not match the internal one, you don't get a signal.

Make sure that the polarity of your pins is correct.  You can NOT
arbitrarily swap them.

Try connecting to the green pins instead.  If the internal cable is a
color cable, the signal will be on the green pins.

Good luck!

