>denny

You have to add the memory SIMMs in pairs.

There are two kinds of memory option:
 8 MB SIMMs (16 MB kit)
32 MB SIMMs (64 MB kit)

Maximum memory is 4 kits, 256 MB.

Memory loading rules:

1. 32 MB kits must be installed before 8 MB kits.  (This lets the FW
arrange the memory with no holes in the address space.)

2. Do not skip any slots.


The memory specs I have (from the system programmer's manual) are as follows:

The 8 MB SIMM is 2Mx36 bits (32 data bits, 4 parity bits) using 1Mx4bit
DRAM chips.

The 32 MB SIMM is 8Mx36 bits (32 data bits, 4 parity bits) using 4Mx4bit
DRAM chips.



The memory configuration hardware in this system is extremely simple. 
Each of the 4 memory banks has 1 bit, which tells the hardware whether the
bank contains a 8 MB or a 32 MB kit.  There's no specific representation
for an empty memory bank; the FW has to figure that out by trial and
error.  That is why the configuration rules are so inflexible.


